Package: forecastsuite
Title: Multi-Model Time Series Forecasting Toolkit and Local App
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: person("Mukul", "Maheshwari", email = "ryan00700@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1918-5100"))
Description: Extends the 'Forecast Dashboard' workflow, which was built around
    'Prophet' (an additive regression forecasting model, Taylor and Letham
    (2018) <doi:10.1080/00031305.2017.1380080>) and ARIMA (AutoRegressive
    Integrated Moving Average, Hyndman and Khandakar (2008)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v027.i03>), with a pluggable model registry. The
    registry covers ARIMA, SARIMA (Seasonal ARIMA), ETS (Error, Trend, Seasonal
    exponential smoothing), TBATS (Trigonometric seasonality, Box-Cox
    transformation, ARMA errors, Trend and Seasonal components, De Livera,
    Hyndman and Snyder (2011) <doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.tm09771>), NNETAR (Neural
    Network AutoRegression), Holt-Winters exponential smoothing (Winters
    (1960) <doi:10.1287/mnsc.6.3.324>), and, optionally, 'Prophet' and LSTM
    (Long Short-Term Memory network, Hochreiter and Schmidhuber (1997)
    <doi:10.1162/neco.1997.9.8.1735>) through the 'prophet' and 'torch'
    packages. Forecast accuracy is summarised with MASE (Mean Absolute Scaled
    Error, Hyndman and Koehler (2006) <doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2006.03.001>),
    sMAPE (symmetric Mean Absolute Percentage Error) and RMSE (Root Mean
    Squared Error). A bundled local 'shiny' application exposes all models
    without the hosted application's memory-conserving constraints.
